    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d194">

                <pb facs="0361" n="229" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv01/pg229"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00116 E. W./6–2945</note>
                <head>No. 194 <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the British
                        Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Halifax</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-07">July 7, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Lord Halifax</hi>: I have your letter of
                    June 29<anchor n="1" xml:id="d194-f1"/> proposing that the subject of “war
                    criminals” be discussed at the next meeting of Heads of Governments.</p>
                <p>The question is being given careful consideration by this Government. Much will
                    depend undoubtedly on the discussions now taking place in London between
                    representatives of the British, United States, French and Soviet
                    Governments.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Joseph C. Grew</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
